WEBVTT

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:04.220
Universal Century 0001.

00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:06.880
As the curtain rose on this new era,

00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:09.930
Laplace, the prime minister's residence,
exploded.

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:13.220
This was history's worst act of terrorism,

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:16.010
carried out
by an anti-Federation organization.

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:21.630
Of the perpetrators,
Syam was the sole survivor.

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:24.090
And so, LaPlace's Box fell into his hands

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:26.180
and his life would be forever changed
because of it.

00:00:27.970 --> 00:00:30.130
Almost a century has passed.

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:34.340
Syam, the founder of the Vist Foundation,
has decided to hand over Laplace's Box,

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:38.630
which is rumored to be able to
overturn the Federation.

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:41.720
Thus, he hopes to
break the stagnant status quo of the times.

00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:45.380
Meanwhile Banagher Links,

00:00:45.430 --> 00:00:48.340
a student attending
the Anaheim Electronics Industrial College

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:50.970
at the colony Industrial 7,

00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:54.510
has a fateful encounter with
a green-eyed girl falling from the sky.

00:00:56.180 --> 00:00:58.340
Prevent it? Prevent what?

00:00:58.380 --> 00:00:59.550
War.

00:01:00.930 --> 00:01:03.090
The girl, who calls herself Audrey,

00:01:03.130 --> 00:01:06.510
visits Cardeas Vist,
the current head of the Vist Foundation,

00:01:06.550 --> 00:01:09.840
to prevent the transfer of Laplace's Box.

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:12.630
But negotiations for the handover
of the Box proceed regardless.

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:17.720
Just then, the Londo Bell unit
of the Earth Federation Forces

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:20.220
seizes control of the colony
to prevent the handover of the Box.

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:23.050
The negotiations break down amid the chaos.

00:01:23.090 --> 00:01:26.630
Cardeas, who is actually Banagher's father,

00:01:26.680 --> 00:01:31.340
entrusts him with the Unicorn Gundam,
the key to Laplace's Box.

00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:33.130
Father...

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:35.680
I'm sorry, Mom.

00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:38.130
I must...

00:01:40.930 --> 00:01:42.010
...go!

00:01:43.430 --> 00:01:48.180
Banagher uses the Unicorn Gundam
to fend off the Sleeves mobile suit.

00:01:48.220 --> 00:01:51.760
He is retrieved by the Londo Bell warship
the Nahel Argama.

00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:55.590
Here, he's reunited with Audrey,
who happens to be aboard the ship.

00:01:56.510 --> 00:02:00.880
Let's see... Let's test the performance
of your new Gundam.

00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:06.430
However, the Nahel Argama is attacked
by the Neo Zeon leader Full Frontal,

00:02:06.470 --> 00:02:09.180
who is pursuing the Unicorn Gundam.

00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:12.130
The Nahel Argama is overwhelmed
by the fighting strength of Frontal,

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:16.090
who is said to be
the second coming of the Red Comet.

00:02:16.130 --> 00:02:19.840
Audrey, who has now been revealed
to be the Zeon princess Mineva Zabi,

00:02:19.880 --> 00:02:22.550
is taken hostage by the ship's crew.

00:02:22.590 --> 00:02:27.470
If we take down that red mobile suit, then
you won't need Audrey as a hostage, right?

00:02:27.510 --> 00:02:28.430
I'll do it!

00:02:28.470 --> 00:02:31.090
Banagher confronts Frontal,

00:02:31.130 --> 00:02:35.970
but is captured and taken to
the Neo Zeon resource satellite Palau.

00:02:36.630 --> 00:02:38.720
Here he meets with Frontal,

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:41.300
and those there remind him that
he himself has taken the life of another,

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:43.630
even though it was in a combat situation.

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:47.180
And from the Sleeves pilot Marida Cruz,

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:50.050
Banagher learns about the hopes and dreams
of the space colonists.

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:53.550
Palau soon
becomes a battlefield as an operation

00:02:53.590 --> 00:02:57.340
begins to rescue Banagher
and the Unicorn Gundam begins,

00:02:57.380 --> 00:03:00.220
and Banagher is
forced to face Marida in battle.

00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:03.430
Ple Twelve.
That is her name.

00:03:03.470 --> 00:03:05.630
This is...
This is all too sad.

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:08.300
Kindness alone can't save people.

00:03:09.010 --> 00:03:11.680
It can't erase sin
or wash away the impurities.

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:14.510
Thanks to the resonance
between the two Newtypes,

00:03:14.550 --> 00:03:17.090
Banagher sees into Marida's heart.

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:21.380
Capturing her and the Kshatriya,
he returns to the Nahel Argama.

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:27.010
Meanwhile Riddhe Marcenas,
who has become a Federation Forces pilot

00:03:27.050 --> 00:03:30.630
even though he is the eldest son
of a political dynasty,

00:03:30.680 --> 00:03:34.800
realizes what Mineva wants
and finds a new resolve within himself.

00:05:08.840 --> 00:05:09.010
The NZ-666 Kshatriya.

00:05:09.010 --> 00:05:11.800
The NZ-666 Kshatriya.
(LAPLACE, WHERE IT ALL BEGAN)

00:05:11.800 --> 00:05:12.800
Judging from the model number,
it's probably made by Neo Zeon.
(LAPLACE, WHERE IT ALL BEGAN)

00:05:12.800 --> 00:05:14.720
Judging from the model number,
it's probably made by Neo Zeon.

00:05:15.470 --> 00:05:18.590
There's a psycho-frame installed
around the cockpit,

00:05:18.630 --> 00:05:20.260
but it's an old type.

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:23.550
I bet they repurposed
a prototype that was supplied

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:25.880
by Anaheim back during
Char's rebellion.

00:05:27.510 --> 00:05:28.680
Captain Otto?

00:05:30.470 --> 00:05:33.050
You say that only Granada
on the moon

00:05:33.090 --> 00:05:35.300
has psycho-frame
manufacturing facilities?

00:05:35.340 --> 00:05:36.260
Yes, sir.

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:39.340
Since development of the technology
was officially halted,

00:05:39.380 --> 00:05:42.380
they're completely responsible for it,
including maintaining its secrecy.

00:05:42.430 --> 00:05:44.340
Why was it halted?

00:05:44.380 --> 00:05:47.430
I hear it was because there were
just too many unknowns.

00:05:47.930 --> 00:05:51.840
Even with the Unicorn, it looks like
the exposed psycho-frame

00:05:51.880 --> 00:05:55.510
is glowing when the NT-D activates
and the armor separates, right?

00:05:55.550 --> 00:05:59.840
We don't know why it glows,
and we're the ones who built it.

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:04.010
And sometimes that glow can be
converted into physical energy.

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:07.430
Um... I didn't see any
of the combat records,

00:06:08.050 --> 00:06:11.130
but it certainly was a
one-sided fight, wasn't it?

00:06:12.050 --> 00:06:15.010
Captain!
Message from sickbay.

00:06:15.050 --> 00:06:16.720
The prisoner's vitals have stabilized.

00:06:17.970 --> 00:06:19.380
Aside from her external injuries,

00:06:19.430 --> 00:06:22.930
she appears to be rather weak,
so it's still too soon to question her.

00:06:22.970 --> 00:06:27.220
What are all these scars from burns
and lacerations all over her body?

00:06:29.380 --> 00:06:34.470
From what Dr. Hasan says,
her reproductive system is also...

00:06:36.180 --> 00:06:38.760
In the closing days of
the First Neo Zeon War,

00:06:38.800 --> 00:06:41.840
a Newtype Corps made up of clones
was sent into battle,

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:44.630
but they were supposed to
have all been wiped out.

00:06:44.680 --> 00:06:48.680
But one of them survived, and this
is what became of her, huh?

00:06:50.090 --> 00:06:52.220
We'll leave her questioning
to Headquarters.

00:06:52.260 --> 00:06:53.470
Understood.

00:06:58.470 --> 00:07:00.430
I hope that this is the last- -

00:07:00.470 --> 00:07:03.470
Detour we'll have to make?
I hope so, too.

00:07:03.510 --> 00:07:06.050
I don't think that
will be necessary.

00:07:06.090 --> 00:07:08.300
She's a cyber-Newtype,
isn't she?

00:07:08.340 --> 00:07:11.130
If she doesn't get her medication,
won't she go berserk?

00:07:11.180 --> 00:07:15.090
She's the type that was genetically
designed from the ground up,

00:07:15.130 --> 00:07:17.180
so there's no need to suppress
her immune response.

00:07:17.220 --> 00:07:18.430
But she- -

00:07:18.470 --> 00:07:22.300
Her emotional state also seems stable,
and besides, her injuries are severe.

00:07:22.340 --> 00:07:25.590
As a doctor, I can't consent to
putting her in a straitjacket.

00:07:25.630 --> 00:07:28.260
But she's a Neo Zeon, remember?

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:30.380
She might even try to
hurt you, Doctor!

00:07:30.430 --> 00:07:32.430
Ms. Marida would never do that!

00:07:32.470 --> 00:07:35.430
Banagher...
I didn't know you were there.

00:07:35.470 --> 00:07:37.180
How do you feel?

00:07:38.470 --> 00:07:40.760
How can you put an injured person
in a straitjacket?

00:07:40.800 --> 00:07:43.300
This is none of your concern.

00:07:43.340 --> 00:07:46.680
Why would you do that?
Ms. Marida's an officer.

00:07:46.720 --> 00:07:50.300
There are rules that govern the
treatment of prisoners, aren't there?

00:07:50.340 --> 00:07:52.220
The Sleeves are terrorists.

00:07:52.260 --> 00:07:54.470
Even if she's an officer,
she's still a criminal.

00:07:54.510 --> 00:07:55.510
But she's- -

00:07:55.550 --> 00:07:58.510
Were you brainwashed
at Palau or something?

00:07:58.550 --> 00:08:01.220
She's the pilot of that quad-wing!

00:08:01.260 --> 00:08:04.840
She's the person responsible for all
the destruction at your own colony.

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:08.380
And there's no telling how many of
our people have been killed by her.

00:08:10.720 --> 00:08:14.380
But... If you start out making
assumptions like that, you'll- -

00:08:14.430 --> 00:08:18.550
We'll put her under guard.
Please notify us when you move her.

00:08:18.590 --> 00:08:19.760
Roger that.

00:08:23.180 --> 00:08:27.300
Think about it. After all,
even Ensign Riddhe didn't come back.

00:08:28.720 --> 00:08:31.260
What are cyber-Newtypes, anyway?

00:08:31.300 --> 00:08:33.430
The product of a delusion.

00:08:33.470 --> 00:08:36.760
That one might be able to create
Newtypes artificially.

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:38.840
To make a long story short,
that was the sophistry they used

00:08:38.880 --> 00:08:42.340
to violate their ethics so they
could create human weapons.

00:08:45.760 --> 00:08:47.630
You know the basic
Newtype concept?

00:08:47.680 --> 00:08:50.220
Yes. It says that when humanity
moved into space,

00:08:50.260 --> 00:08:52.590
we'd become able to understand
each other without misconceptions.

00:08:52.630 --> 00:08:54.430
That's right.

00:08:54.470 --> 00:08:59.630
But if we all became like that, wars
ought to become a thing of the past...

00:09:01.340 --> 00:09:03.720
Somebody once said
that the reason

00:09:03.760 --> 00:09:06.550
mankind's wars never end
was because we're stuck

00:09:06.590 --> 00:09:09.220
on the threshold of a new
stage of evolution.

00:09:10.010 --> 00:09:13.430
If there really is a chance for us
to become Newtypes,

00:09:13.470 --> 00:09:16.760
he said cyber-Newtype research
should be allowed.

00:09:16.800 --> 00:09:19.590
If we leave evolution
to Mother Nature,

00:09:19.630 --> 00:09:23.180
humanity will kill itself off first.

00:09:23.220 --> 00:09:25.510
I think that's a sad way
of looking at things.

00:09:25.550 --> 00:09:28.630
I agree. That's why we have to work
at understanding each other

00:09:28.680 --> 00:09:31.760
with the abilities we have right now,
limited as they are.

00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:38.010
Our roles have reversed,
I see.

00:09:42.430 --> 00:09:44.220
Don't stare at me like that.

00:09:44.880 --> 00:09:48.720
It's all a bit hazy.
How did all that happen?

00:09:48.760 --> 00:09:51.300
You must have been swallowed up
by the machine.

00:09:51.340 --> 00:09:53.510
A psycommu backflow.

00:09:53.550 --> 00:09:57.590
You think you're controlling it,
but it suddenly starts controlling you.

00:09:58.720 --> 00:10:01.590
I sensed powerful negative intent.

00:10:01.630 --> 00:10:05.590
That was probably the instinct of the
system embedded in the Gundam.

00:10:05.630 --> 00:10:07.930
To seek out Newtypes
and destroy them.

00:10:08.510 --> 00:10:11.050
Even if those Newtypes
are artificial ones.

00:10:12.220 --> 00:10:16.470
A machine doesn't have the capability
to discern natural from artificial.

00:10:16.510 --> 00:10:18.260
But people are another story.

00:10:18.970 --> 00:10:20.880
They can sense the difference.

00:10:20.930 --> 00:10:22.380
But even you...

00:10:22.430 --> 00:10:24.340
I have a Master.

00:10:26.090 --> 00:10:32.090
Even if I was created artificially,
my entire being is devoted to him.

00:10:32.680 --> 00:10:37.800
I hope for what he hopes for,
and I oppose what he opposes.

00:10:38.800 --> 00:10:44.260
But that's a curse,
killing yourself bit by bit like that.

00:10:44.300 --> 00:10:46.130
I saw inside you.

00:10:46.760 --> 00:10:49.680
You and I might be
two of a kind.

00:10:50.300 --> 00:10:51.930
What do you mean by that?

00:10:53.430 --> 00:10:57.260
If I don't look at it that way,
losing to you would be humiliating.

00:10:57.300 --> 00:10:59.430
Still, the Gundam stopped.

00:10:59.470 --> 00:11:05.340
Your will... the foundation inside you
forced the system into submission.

00:11:05.380 --> 00:11:06.680
Foundation?

00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:11.680
Those like me don't have that.
It's what lets us merge with machines.

00:11:11.720 --> 00:11:13.470
- Ms. Marid- -
- Never mind me.

00:11:15.590 --> 00:11:19.510
Banagher, no matter what sort
of realities you're forced to confront,

00:11:19.550 --> 00:11:22.430
keep saying,
"Even so..."

00:11:22.470 --> 00:11:24.800
Never lose sight of who you are.

00:11:25.680 --> 00:11:27.880
That's the foundation
of who you are.

00:11:27.930 --> 00:11:32.840
The power that awakens
that other system,

00:11:32.880 --> 00:11:35.340
the one sleeping
in that Gundam, it...

00:11:36.430 --> 00:11:39.470
Laplace's Box was entrusted
to it so it could- -

00:11:42.680 --> 00:11:43.880
Ms. Marida!

00:11:43.930 --> 00:11:45.630
- Ms. Marida!
- What's wrong?

00:11:59.590 --> 00:12:01.720
Banagher, not happy.

00:12:06.470 --> 00:12:08.880
Looks like the Captain and his
officers are keeping it secret

00:12:09.970 --> 00:12:12.970
that the Zeons' princess disappeared.

00:12:13.010 --> 00:12:18.090
I just wish we could tell Ensign Mihiro
that Ensign Riddhe is alive.

00:12:18.130 --> 00:12:19.800
I didn't know they
were an item.

00:12:19.840 --> 00:12:22.090
- An item, an item!
- I'm not really sure, but still.

00:12:22.130 --> 00:12:24.720
I wonder if she made it
to Earth all right?

00:12:24.760 --> 00:12:26.720
He's with her,
so she'll be fine.

00:12:27.590 --> 00:12:29.800
You don't really
seem like yourself.

00:12:31.430 --> 00:12:34.340
You didn't used to be this
cool-headed about her.

00:12:56.010 --> 00:12:58.510
Begging your pardon, sir!

00:13:03.720 --> 00:13:08.010
Master, we've just received an urgent
communique from the military.

00:13:08.050 --> 00:13:09.880
Young Master Riddhe has...

00:13:14.640 --> 00:13:17.470
Princess Mineva has
gone down to Earth?

00:13:17.510 --> 00:13:20.310
The intel comes from a sympathizer
within the Federation Government.

00:13:20.350 --> 00:13:24.560
He says a mobile suit used Assembly
privilege to cross their defensive lines.

00:13:24.600 --> 00:13:26.260
She was likely aboard.

00:13:26.310 --> 00:13:28.060
You don't think it was a diversion?

00:13:28.100 --> 00:13:29.720
The Mock Trojan Horse's position?

00:13:29.760 --> 00:13:32.640
Approaching geosynchronous orbit, sir.

00:13:32.680 --> 00:13:36.510
As I thought. So, they're headed for
the designated coordinates, are they?

00:13:36.560 --> 00:13:39.180
I believe this time
we'll chance upon something.

00:13:39.220 --> 00:13:42.600
It's far too perfect a place
to break the La+ seal.

00:13:44.140 --> 00:13:45.640
The Klimt.

00:13:45.680 --> 00:13:49.640
A shuttle used by the Vist Foundation
to transport works of art, eh?

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:52.260
They're just doing an orbital
sightseeing flight

00:13:52.310 --> 00:13:54.100
above the equator
without even accelerating.

00:13:54.140 --> 00:13:57.810
If we're assuming that they're meeting
with someone, it must be with...

00:13:59.350 --> 00:14:03.100
Whatever their objective is, if they're
planning an orbital rendezvous,

00:14:03.140 --> 00:14:04.600
it'll leave them vulnerable.

00:14:04.640 --> 00:14:06.140
Do we attack, sir?

00:14:06.180 --> 00:14:09.060
We'll be scraping atmosphere.
Can we pull it off?

00:14:09.100 --> 00:14:10.260
We'll sure try.

00:14:10.310 --> 00:14:12.350
Laplace's Box notwithstanding,

00:14:12.390 --> 00:14:16.430
we can't leave Marida to stew aboard
the Mock Trojan Horse, can we?

00:14:16.470 --> 00:14:18.560
Flaste, the helm's yours!

00:14:18.600 --> 00:14:23.010
W-Wait!
Are you sure, Captain?

00:14:28.010 --> 00:14:29.850
I suppose he's right.

00:14:32.890 --> 00:14:37.220
The Nahel Argama will conduct an
inspection of the coordinate airspace.

00:14:37.260 --> 00:14:39.850
Before the Unicorn
is shipped off to Luna II,

00:14:39.890 --> 00:14:43.060
information regarding the key
to Laplace's Box will be- -

00:14:43.100 --> 00:14:46.600
You aren't looking well.
Is there a problem?

00:14:46.640 --> 00:14:52.220
No... It's just that after all these
battles, the men are exhausted.

00:14:52.260 --> 00:14:57.930
Well... I was wondering if this matter
should have been left to another unit.

00:14:58.430 --> 00:15:00.810
You almost look as if you've
become attached to them.

00:15:02.010 --> 00:15:05.140
Once you've landed on Earth,
feel free to relax a while.

00:15:05.180 --> 00:15:06.560
Landed on Earth?

00:15:06.600 --> 00:15:09.310
I've chartered a transport.

00:15:09.350 --> 00:15:12.470
Use it to take the cyber-Newtype
who's being held prisoner

00:15:12.510 --> 00:15:15.180
aboard the Nahel Argama
to Augusta in North America.

00:15:15.220 --> 00:15:17.470
Augusta?

00:15:17.510 --> 00:15:18.640
Right.

00:15:18.680 --> 00:15:20.640
The labs there
have been shut down,

00:15:20.680 --> 00:15:24.180
but I'm told that the facilities needed
for readjustments are still there.

00:15:24.220 --> 00:15:26.810
What do you have in mind?

00:15:26.850 --> 00:15:30.970
If Grandfather had simply told me
the location of the Box,

00:15:31.010 --> 00:15:34.510
I wouldn't have to resort to
such underhanded methods.

00:15:36.560 --> 00:15:40.560
I don't know what Grandfather
and Cardeas' goal was,

00:15:40.600 --> 00:15:44.390
but if the Box is lost, so are
the Foundation's fortunes.

00:15:44.430 --> 00:15:47.100
There is activity within
the Federation Government

00:15:47.140 --> 00:15:50.220
to try to gain the Box for itself
in anticipation of that loss.

00:15:50.930 --> 00:15:54.600
This is no time to let petty sympathies
get the better of you.

00:15:54.640 --> 00:15:58.350
Laplace's Box is our very lifeline.

00:15:59.100 --> 00:16:02.140
I'm counting on you, Alberto.

00:16:02.390 --> 00:16:03.970
I won't do it!

00:16:04.010 --> 00:16:06.310
That wasn't a request.

00:16:06.350 --> 00:16:11.060
If the Unicorn is piloted through the
coordinates given by the La+ Program,

00:16:11.100 --> 00:16:14.470
there's a high probability that another
seal on the program will be broken.

00:16:14.510 --> 00:16:16.260
I'll ride with you.

00:16:16.310 --> 00:16:20.060
I want you to take the suit to
the appropriate coordinates.

00:16:20.100 --> 00:16:21.220
That's an order.

00:16:21.260 --> 00:16:24.760
You saw it, right? You saw what
happened to it at Palau, didn't you?

00:16:27.930 --> 00:16:31.810
I'm not a soldier, so I shouldn't
have to take orders from you.

00:16:31.850 --> 00:16:35.850
No, you aren't obliged to obey me.
But you do have a responsibility.

00:16:35.890 --> 00:16:38.850
You've intervened in battle situations
three times now.

00:16:39.430 --> 00:16:41.680
With a powerful weapon.

00:16:41.720 --> 00:16:43.970
Lives may have been saved
because of you,

00:16:44.930 --> 00:16:46.890
but lives were lost, too.

00:16:48.680 --> 00:16:54.640
You're already interfering in the destinies
of a lot of people, friend and foe alike.

00:16:54.680 --> 00:16:57.010
You need to take
responsibility for that.

00:16:57.060 --> 00:16:58.810
How do I do that?

00:16:58.850 --> 00:17:00.510
By seeing this through.

00:17:01.680 --> 00:17:03.890
Keep fighting until
I die, is that it?

00:17:03.930 --> 00:17:07.430
Or am I supposed to stay on this crazy
treasure hunt to the bitter end?

00:17:07.470 --> 00:17:09.350
Think that over for yourself.

00:17:09.390 --> 00:17:12.810
All you're doing now is running away
from the troubles in front of you.

00:17:12.850 --> 00:17:15.100
But people are going to die!

00:17:15.140 --> 00:17:17.850
What's this "responsibility" that
means I have to kill people?

00:17:17.890 --> 00:17:20.810
I can't make up my mind about
something like that so easily!

00:17:31.680 --> 00:17:33.680
Don't be so hard on him.

00:17:37.430 --> 00:17:40.680
They have to look at things
that way, it's their job.

00:17:48.220 --> 00:17:50.560
Is something the matter,
Commander?

00:17:51.180 --> 00:17:53.810
No, I was just thinking that
if I had a son of my own,

00:17:53.850 --> 00:17:56.850
I would've experienced these
feelings a long time ago.

00:18:00.220 --> 00:18:04.220
I haven't been this close since that
field trip we went on in grade school.

00:18:04.260 --> 00:18:08.890
This is the first thing that comes
to mind when I hear "Laplace's Box"...

00:18:08.930 --> 00:18:12.390
Latitude, zero.
Longitude, zero. Altitude, 200 kilometers.

00:18:12.430 --> 00:18:14.680
The wreckage of Laplace,
the prime minister's residence,

00:18:14.720 --> 00:18:17.260
passes that point
once a day without fail.

00:18:17.310 --> 00:18:21.010
I don't think we overlooked something
that was right under our noses- -

00:18:21.060 --> 00:18:24.760
In my day, it had already been removed
from the school tour list.

00:18:24.810 --> 00:18:28.060
Captain, Commander,
thank you for looking after us.

00:18:30.430 --> 00:18:34.140
I won't play nice and say
the pleasure was all ours.

00:18:34.180 --> 00:18:36.310
You brought us
nothing but trouble.

00:18:36.350 --> 00:18:39.010
We won't be forgetting that face
of yours anytime soon.

00:18:39.930 --> 00:18:42.970
I regret that I won't be able
to observe the investigation...

00:18:44.560 --> 00:18:47.510
May fortune continue to smile
upon you in battle.

00:18:47.560 --> 00:18:49.060
Good day.

00:18:53.390 --> 00:18:56.600
That's odd. He was always
so obsessed with the Box.

00:18:56.640 --> 00:18:59.260
In the end, he's just
a lackey to the mighty.

00:18:59.310 --> 00:19:03.390
Anaheim will get the investigation
results via Staff HQ.

00:19:03.430 --> 00:19:05.350
Do you suppose
that's all there is to it?

00:19:06.180 --> 00:19:10.680
It's not normal to entrust the transport
of a prisoner to a civilian ship.

00:19:10.720 --> 00:19:15.260
For HQ to okay that, what do you
suppose they have in mind for her?

00:19:15.310 --> 00:19:19.260
Their cover story is that Luna II
doesn't have the facilities

00:19:19.310 --> 00:19:21.720
to care for a cyber-Newtype.

00:19:22.810 --> 00:19:24.720
RX-0, launching.

00:19:29.390 --> 00:19:31.560
He feels like
piloting it now, eh?

00:19:32.720 --> 00:19:36.970
The Nahel Argama is currently
positioned in low Earth orbit.

00:19:37.010 --> 00:19:39.470
In principle, it's no different
from operating in space,

00:19:39.510 --> 00:19:41.850
but if you don't constantly maintain
the prescribed speed,

00:19:41.890 --> 00:19:44.850
you'll get pulled in by gravity
in the blink of an eye, so be careful.

00:19:44.890 --> 00:19:45.970
Right.

00:19:47.850 --> 00:19:51.010
When we were told to attack
Palau on our own,

00:19:51.060 --> 00:19:53.560
I'll be honest, we were already
weary to the bone.

00:19:55.470 --> 00:19:58.510
But then Commander Daguza spoke up.

00:19:58.560 --> 00:20:03.430
He called it a hostage rescue operation.
He said we owed you one.

00:20:04.010 --> 00:20:09.640
He's trying to carry out the responsibility
that people should have for one another.

00:20:12.720 --> 00:20:14.390
- What is it?
- Nothing.

00:20:14.430 --> 00:20:17.930
Do you ever feel uncertainty,
Mr. Daguza?

00:20:17.970 --> 00:20:22.010
I'm a cog, a part of a vast machine
called the Federation.

00:20:22.060 --> 00:20:25.100
I carry out the duties
I'm given, that's all.

00:20:25.140 --> 00:20:27.760
I can't be certain
about anything.

00:20:27.810 --> 00:20:29.760
Not even who's my friend
and who's my enemy.

00:20:30.640 --> 00:20:34.390
A person like that isn't qualified
to pick up a weapon, is he?

00:20:34.430 --> 00:20:36.890
I never wanted to get in
this thing ever again.

00:20:36.930 --> 00:20:39.430
Not even if it meant
letting him down.

00:20:41.970 --> 00:20:43.970
Think of it this way.

00:20:44.010 --> 00:20:48.390
You have people around you that
you have to take responsibility for.

00:20:48.430 --> 00:20:50.350
You mean Takuya and Micott?

00:20:50.390 --> 00:20:51.890
After we get back to Luna II,

00:20:51.930 --> 00:20:55.890
what happens to those two
will depend on what we report.

00:20:55.930 --> 00:20:59.010
What that report says
will depend on your actions.

00:20:59.060 --> 00:21:00.890
Taking hostages again, huh?

00:21:00.930 --> 00:21:02.760
Take it however you want.

00:21:02.810 --> 00:21:05.850
You're in a position to be
able to alter their fates.

00:21:05.890 --> 00:21:10.470
In that sense, right here and now,
you're making the right choice.

00:21:11.930 --> 00:21:13.850
Another launch confirmed.

00:21:13.890 --> 00:21:17.100
It seems to be on a rendezvous trajectory
with the suits that launched earlier.

00:21:17.140 --> 00:21:18.720
Is it that Gundam?

00:21:18.760 --> 00:21:21.810
Unable to confirm.
No response on psycho-monitor.

00:21:21.850 --> 00:21:24.930
So we can't trace it in its
one-horn configuration, huh?

00:21:25.510 --> 00:21:27.470
Status of the Foundation ship?

00:21:27.510 --> 00:21:29.390
On a contact course.

00:21:29.430 --> 00:21:32.970
Assuming the Mock Trojan Horse
decelerates to orbital velocity,

00:21:33.640 --> 00:21:36.350
estimated time to contact is
approximately ten minutes.

00:21:36.390 --> 00:21:40.220
360 km directly above the equator.
East longitude 15 degrees, 28 minutes.

00:21:40.760 --> 00:21:45.510
Just as you've heard it. It looks
like their plan is to rendezvous

00:21:45.560 --> 00:21:47.510
and then inspect the
designated coordinates.

00:21:47.560 --> 00:21:51.600
Our opening will come when their suits
are away at the Laplace wreckage.

00:21:51.640 --> 00:21:52.680
Roger that.

00:21:52.720 --> 00:21:56.010
The Garencieres Team has finally
gotten a job that's up its alley.

00:21:56.060 --> 00:22:00.180
Don't get too ambitious. Remember,
you have a family waiting at home.

00:22:00.220 --> 00:22:03.390
I understand. I'll bring Marida back
safe and sound, don't you worry.

00:22:04.640 --> 00:22:06.010
I'm counting on you.

00:23:38.310 --> 00:23:41.600
Next time, on Mobile Suit Gundam Unicorn

00:23:41.640 --> 00:23:43.310
RETRIBUTION

00:23:45.060 --> 00:23:48.470
awaken the Newtype that lies within you.
